# Phase 8 — Real-Time Group Chat & Live Collaboration

## 📌 Overview

Phase 8 adds **real-time communication and collaboration** to TripMate.

The goal of this phase was to allow members of the same trip to communicate instantly without refreshing the page. The chat system supports real-time text messaging and is designed around **Socket.IO**, with MongoDB used for persistent message storage.

The phase also introduces the foundation for **real-time location sharing**, allowing trip members to share their current location while travelling.

This phase helped me understand how a modern real-time web application works beyond the traditional request-response model of REST APIs.

---

## 🎯 Objectives

The main objectives of Phase 8 were:

* Build a real-time group chat for trip members.
* Allow messages to appear instantly for all connected members.
* Persist chat messages in MongoDB.
* Authenticate Socket.IO connections using the existing session-based authentication.
* Restrict chat access to members of the corresponding trip.
* Load previous messages when a user opens the chat.
* Handle users joining and leaving trip-specific chat rooms.
* Implement real-time location sharing as the foundation for live trip tracking.
* Understand the difference between REST APIs and WebSocket-based communication.

