# 🧠 What Problem Does Socket.IO Solve?

Normal REST APIs follow a request-response model.

For example:

```text
User A
  |
  | POST /api/trips/123/messages
  ↓
Backend
  |
  ↓
MongoDB
```

The backend stores the message and sends a response back to User A.

But User B does not automatically know that a new message was created.

User B would have to repeatedly call:

```text
GET /api/trips/123/messages
```

This approach is inefficient for real-time communication.

With Socket.IO:

```text
User A
   |
   |  "Hello!"
   ↓
Socket.IO Server
   |
   ├──────────→ User A
   |
   └──────────→ User B
```

The server can immediately push the new message to all connected members.

This creates a real-time chat experience.

