# 🔐 Authentication

TripMate uses **session-based authentication**, not JWT.

The same authentication system used by the REST APIs is also used for Socket.IO connections.

When a user logs in:

```text
User
 ↓
POST /api/auth/login
 ↓
Express Session
 ↓
Session stored in MongoDB
```

The browser receives the session cookie.

When the Socket.IO connection is established, the server checks the user's session.

Conceptually:

```text
Browser
   |
   | Session Cookie
   ↓
Socket.IO Server
   |
   ↓
Session Validation
   |
   ├── Invalid → Reject connection
   |
   └── Valid → Identify user
```

This means the socket connection is associated with an authenticated TripMate user.

