# 🚪 Trip-Specific Chat Rooms

One of the important concepts learned in this phase was **Socket.IO rooms**.

Every trip has its own room.

For example:

```text
Trip ID: 64abc123

Socket Room:
trip:64abc123
```

When a member opens the chat:

```text
User
  ↓
Socket Connection
  ↓
Join Trip Room
  ↓
trip:64abc123
```

Now messages for this trip can be broadcast only to users inside that room.

Example:

```text
Trip A
 ├── User 1
 ├── User 2
 └── User 3

Trip B
 ├── User 4
 └── User 5
```

A message from User 1 is sent only to:

```text
Trip A room
```

It is never broadcast to Trip B.

This provides logical isolation between different trips.

