# ⚡ Real-Time Event Flow

Socket.IO works using events.

The basic idea is:

```javascript
socket.emit("eventName", data);
```

and:

```javascript
socket.on("eventName", callback);
```

For example:

```text
Client
  |
  | emit("sendMessage")
  ↓
Server
  |
  | emit/broadcast message
  ↓
Other Clients
```

This is different from normal HTTP APIs where communication is generally initiated by the client.

