# 📍 Live Location Sharing

Another important part of Phase 8 is the foundation for **live location sharing**.

The browser provides the user's location using the Geolocation API.

Conceptually:

```text
Browser GPS/Location
        ↓
navigator.geolocation
        ↓
Latitude + Longitude
        ↓
Socket.IO
        ↓
shareLocation event
        ↓
Trip Room
        ↓
Other Trip Members
```

The server broadcasts location updates to the other members.

For example:

```text
User A
lat: 26.1445
lng: 91.7362
       ↓
Socket.IO
       ↓
Trip Room
       ↓
User B / User C
```

The location updates are intended to be displayed on the map from the Map module.

---

# 🚫 Why Live Location Is Not Stored Continuously

A user's location can change every few seconds.

If every location update were stored in MongoDB:

```text
1 update / 5 sec
= 12 updates / minute
= 720 updates / hour
= 17,280 updates / day
```

for just one user.

For multiple users, this would create unnecessary database writes.

Therefore the architecture is:

```text
Live Location
     ↓
Socket.IO
     ↓
Broadcast
     ↓
Other Users
```

instead of:

```text
Live Location
     ↓
MongoDB
     ↓
Read MongoDB
     ↓
Other Users
```

This is more suitable for high-frequency temporary data.

---

# 🖼️ Media Sharing Architecture

The chat architecture also supports media messages.

Instead of storing the actual image inside MongoDB, the image is uploaded to **Cloudinary**.

The general flow is:

```text
User selects image
       ↓
Upload image
       ↓
Cloudinary
       ↓
Image URL
       ↓
Socket.IO message
       ↓
MongoDB stores message + URL
       ↓
Other users receive URL
       ↓
Browser loads image
```

This follows an important principle:

> Store large media files in dedicated object/media storage and store their references in the database.

