# 🔒 Security Considerations

Real-time communication also requires authorization.

Simply knowing a Trip ID should not allow anyone to join its chat.

The backend should verify:

```text
Is the user authenticated?
        ↓
Is the user a member of this trip?
        ↓
If yes → allow chat
If no  → reject
```

This prevents unauthorized users from accessing private trip conversations.

The important principle learned here is:

> Authentication tells us who the user is; authorization tells us what that user is allowed to access.

